## Why This Is Asked
The VPN gateway fleet across regions tests basic KCA flows, multi-region trust, and policy binding in a tangible, beginner-friendly setting.

## Key Concepts
- Attestation to regional bootstrap
- CSR enrollment to central KCA with SPIFFE IDs
- Streaming policy updates and TTL-based certs
- Per-tenant policy binding and revocation models

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo flow: enroll CSR, register SPIFFE ID, grant vpn scope
async function enrollGatewayCSR(gw) {
  const csr = await gw.createCSR();
  const id = `spiffe://${gw.region}/vpn/${gw.id}`;
  return enrollToKCA(csr, id, 'vpn');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test reattestation latency under regional outage?
- What metrics ensure policy streaming keeps pace with cert renewal?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical KCA design for mobile field devices in multi-region deployments, focusing on real-world constraints like unreliable networks and urgent revocation needs.

## Key Concepts
- Regional attestation and baseline image trust
- Short-lived TLS certificates with SPIFFE IDs
- Per-app policy binding and code-signing for mobile apps
- Offline revocation checks and audit logs
- Recovery tests for connectivity loss and device loss

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code sketch: enrollment flow
function enrollDevice(device, region){
  attestToRegionalBootstrap(region);
  const cert = requestCertificateFromKCA({region, deviceId: device.id}, TTL_120s, 'techfield');
  bindAppPolicies(cert, device.appId);
  enableOffline_revocation(cert);
}
```

